{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwMul"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.murphySum_mul_σ_subgroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.murphySum_mul_σ_subgroup","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L361-L372","doc":"**Murphy's `x_λ`, from the right.** Together with `σ_mul_murphySum_subgroup` this says\n`x_λ` is a two-sided `q`-eigenvector for every generator of its Young subgroup — which is\nwhat Mathas uses throughout Lemma 3.9 and Lemma 3.12, and what makes `m_{st} =\nT_{d(s)}^* x_λ T_{d(t)}` behave under multiplication on either side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.murphySum_mul_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.murphySum_mul_σ","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L336-L359","doc":"**`x_S · σ_i = q · x_S`** for any finite `S` closed under **left** multiplication by\n`s_i` — the mirror of `σ_mul_murphySum`, and the factor Murphy's `T_{d(t)}` sits against.\nNote the handedness swap: the left-handed statement asks for closure under `w ↦ w · s_i`,\nthis one for closure under `w ↦ s_i · w`. A subgroup has both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.Tw_mul_σ_pair'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.Tw_mul_σ_pair'","kind":"theorem","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L330-L334","doc":"**The right-handed eigenvector, unconditional.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.sw_length_dichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.sw_length_dichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L312-L328","doc":"The **length dichotomy** for a simple reflection: `ℓ(s_i v)` is `ℓ(v) ± 1`, so exactly\none of the two hypotheses of `Tw_mul_σ_pair` holds. This is what makes the right-handed\npair lemma unconditional, matching its left-handed twin `σ_mul_Tw_pair` (whose dichotomy\ncame for free from the concrete descent test). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.simple_eq_sw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.simple_eq_sw","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L305-L310","doc":"`s_i` **is** the `i`-th Coxeter simple reflection of `S_{n+1}`. `permCoxeterSystem` is\nbuilt from `toPerm`'s inverse, so this is `toPerm_simple` read through that. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.Tw_mul_σ_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.Tw_mul_σ_pair","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L270-L302","doc":"**The right-handed eigenvector pair** — the mirror of `σ_mul_Tw_pair`. Whichever of\n`v`, `s_i · v` is the longer, the two-term sum is a `q`-eigenvector for right\nmultiplication by `σ_i`. The dichotomy is supplied by the caller as `h`, which says the\ntwo lengths differ by `ℓ(s_i)` one way or the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.Tw_mul_σ_of_length_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.Tw_mul_σ_of_length_sub","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L248-L268","doc":"**Right multiplication, descending case.** The mirror of `σ_mul_Tw_of_not_lt`: the\nquadratic relation's coefficients appear. The hypothesis is the ascending condition for\n`s_i · v`, which is what \"`s_i` lowers `v`\" means. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.Tw_mul_σ_of_length_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.Tw_mul_σ_of_length_add","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L238-L246","doc":"**Right multiplication, ascending case.** When the lengths add, no coefficients —\nthe mirror of `σ_mul_Tw_of_lt`. One line from `Tw_mul_Tw`, whose convention already\nreverses the order (`T_v · T_w = T_{w v}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.Tw_sw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.Tw_sw","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L231-L236","doc":"`T_{s_i} = σ_i`. Reproved here rather than imported: the corpus's copy lives in\n`QOU.Hecke.TwGramRankOne`, whose Gram machinery this file has no other use for, and the\nproof is two lines from the ascending case of the left-handed table. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.σ_mul_murphySum_subgroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.σ_mul_murphySum_subgroup","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L192-L210","doc":"**The Young-subgroup form — Murphy's `x_λ` proper.**\n\nA Young subgroup `S_λ ≤ S_{n+1}` is generated by the simple reflections it contains, so for\neach such `s_i` it is in particular closed under right multiplication by `s_i`, and this\ncorollary applies. Stating it for an arbitrary subgroup rather than for the Young subgroups\nspecifically costs nothing and avoids having to define the composition-to-subgroup map here:\nwhat the eigenvector property needs is closure, and a subgroup containing `s_i` has it.\n\n`x_λ = Σ_{w ∈ S_λ} T_w` is then a `q`-eigenvector for **every** generator of `S_λ` — which\nis Murphy's defining property, and the hypothesis under which `m_{st} = T_{d(s)}^* x_λ\nT_{d(t)}` is the right object to build a cellular basis on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.σ_mul_murphySum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.σ_mul_murphySum","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L165-L190","doc":"**The defining eigenvector property of the Murphy element**:\n`σ_i · x_S = q · x_S`, whenever `S` is closed under right multiplication by `s_i`.\n\nA Young subgroup containing `s_i` is closed in this sense, so this covers Murphy's `x_λ`\nfor every generator of `S_λ` — but the hypothesis is weaker than being a subgroup, which\nis the honest statement of what the proof uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.murphySum_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.murphySum_empty","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L162-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.murphySum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.murphySum","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L156-L160","doc":"**The Murphy element of a set of permutations**, `x_S = Σ_{w ∈ S} T_w`.  For `S` a\nYoung subgroup `S_λ` this is Murphy's `x_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.σ_mul_Tw_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.σ_mul_Tw_pair","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L130-L154","doc":"**The pair identity — the whole content of this file.**  `T_w + T_{w s_i}` is a\n`q`-eigenvector of `σ_i`, for **every** `w`, with no ascent/descent hypothesis.\n\nWhichever of `w`, `w s_i` ascends at `i`, the other descends, and the two branches of the\nmultiplication rule recombine to the same thing: the ascending one contributes its partner\nwith coefficient `1`, the descending one contributes `(q-1)` of itself and `q` of its\npartner, and `1 + (q-1) = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.mul_sw_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.mul_sw_succ","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L123-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.mul_sw_castSucc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.mul_sw_castSucc","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L118-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.mul_sw_sw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.mul_sw_sw","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L115-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.mul_sw_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.mul_sw_ne","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L109-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.sw_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.sw_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L102-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.sw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy.sw","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeMurphy.lean#L93-L98","doc":"The adjacent transposition `s_i`, as a permutation of `Fin (n+1)`.\n\n`n` is bound implicitly *here* rather than taken from the `variable` block above: that block\ndeclares `n` explicit, which would make this `sw (n) (i)` and silently elaborate `sw i` as\n`sw (n := i)` — `i` read as the rank. ","signatureChunk":0}]}